nodes.body:
@sfc-gh-truwase, Trino brought up some performance concerns:

  • Extra memory/copy: the legacy FP32-master path now uses a persistent host accumulator, even for one backward. Measured with 1,048,576 BF16 values: 2 MiB additional storage and one extra copy per call. Allocation happens once, not every step. The compact FP32 accumulation path bypasses this.
  
I'm going to try to fix it, so the one bwd per update path isn't paying the cost it doesn't need to.

